            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0586" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.515/95: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-19T17:00:00-04:00">April 19, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>189. Your 334, April 1. Shipping costs of $500,000 in small gold bars from the
                    United States to Iran by air would be approximately as follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Packing and trucking $50.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Insurance 4 percent ad valorem, expenses may be included in
                            value.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Freight costs cannot be estimated until transport priority and route
                            are determined.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
